<title>USA: Troy SD, Mich., $86 mln repriced, yields lowered.</title>
<headline>Troy SD, Mich., $86 mln repriced, yields lowered.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>AG Edwards &amp; Sons Inc said Tuesday it repriced Troy School District, Mich.'s $86 million bond deal, lowering yields five basis points in the 2011 through 2013 maturities.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:  </p>
<p>TROY SCHOOL DISTRICT</p>
<p>COUNTY OF OAKLAND, STATE OF MICHIGAN</p>
<p>RE: $86,285,000*</p>
<p>1997 SCHOOL BUILDING &amp; SITE &amp; REFUNDING BONDS</p>
<p>(GENERAL OBLIGATION - UNLIMITED TAX)</p>
<p>MICHIGAN SCHOOL LOAN QUALIFIED</p>
<p>THE VERBAL AWARD HAS BEEN RECEIVED.</p>
<p>THE ACCOUNT IS CLOSED.</p>
<p>PLEASE NOTE REPRICING IN THE 2011 THRU 2013 MATURITY.</p>
<p>FINAL PRICING AS FOLLOWS:</p>
<p>    MOODY'S: Aa2		 S&amp;P: AA</p>
<p>UNDERLYING RATING FOR THE SCHOOL DISTRICT:  AA3/AA-</p>
<p>    DATED: 08/01/1997	  FIRST COUPON: 05/01/1998</p>
<p>DUE: 05/01</p>
